#Sentry weapons - RTS owned, referenced ONLY by
#core/data/scripts/fs2rts_config.lua Station.Sentries.Classes[*].weapon
#
# WHY THESE WERE INVISIBLE FOR SO LONG
# -----------------------------------
# Every entry below once carried `+nocreate`, on the reasoning that the flag
# "ADDS a weapon rather than editing one". It does the exact opposite:
# +nocreate sets create_if_not_found=false (weapons.cpp:790-795), and an entry
# that does not already exist is then skipped wholesale - the engine jumps to
# the next $Name:/#End and returns -1 (weapons.cpp:845-855). `+nocreate` is
# for REDEFINING a weapon retail already has. On a brand-new name it deletes
# the entry, silently.
#
# The file itself always loaded: weapon_init() parses weapons.tbl and then
# parse_modular_table("*-wep.tbm") (weapons.cpp:5157-5159), and this filename
# matches. The evidence that made it look otherwise was real - a headless probe
# saw exactly 90 weapon classes, indices 87-90 all retail - but 90 is also the
# number of $Name: entries in retail weapons.tbl, i.e. the count with all four
# of these discarded. Nothing loaded because nothing was allowed to.
#
# WHY NOTHING CAUGHT IT: an unknown weapon name resolves to an INVALID HANDLE,
# not nil (scripting/api/libs/tables.cpp), so a `weaponClass == nil` guard can
# never fire, and writing that handle into a turret bank is a silent no-op
# (ship_bank.cpp guards on weaponclass > -1). CreateSentry's guard now tests
# isValid() instead. DescribeSentryRange has the same shape and had the same
# bug: it read LifeMax/Speed off the invalid handle, got 0, and fell back to
# option.range - so the HUD tooltip advertised 12,000 m for a gun firing at
# ~1 km. core/tools/test_table_references.py now enforces the engine's rule so
# this cannot be reintroduced.
#
# Do not add +nocreate back. If a future sentry weapon is meant to redefine a
# retail gun instead of adding one, that is a different kind of change and this
# file's reasoning does not apply to it.
#
# REACH is derived from measured engagement geometry, not chosen. Ring p50
# radius is ~4,300 m and the median station-beam standoff is 10,622 m, so
# tier-1 sits at 11,000 m and higher tiers reach further. The engine fires out
# to MIN(lifetime * max_speed, +Weapon Range), and GetSentryWeaponRange reads
# those same two fields off the weapon class, so the tooltip quotes the gun's
# real reach and there is exactly one place the number lives.
#
# NO PRICING CHANGES here. Sentry economics are a separate open question
# (docs/design/defense-balance-position.md).

$Name: RTS Sentry Screen Laser
$Damage: 60
$Shots: 2
$Fire Wait: 0.9
$Velocity: 1000
$Lifetime: 15
+Weapon Range: 11000

$Name: RTS Sentry Flak
$Damage: 90
$Shots: 3
$Fire Wait: 1.1
$Velocity: 1000
$Lifetime: 16
+Weapon Range: 11500

$Name: RTS Sentry Missiles
$Damage: 120
$Shots: 1
$Fire Wait: 1.6
$Velocity: 1000
$Lifetime: 17
+Weapon Range: 12000

$Name: RTS Sentry Beam
$Damage: 150
$Shots: 1
$Fire Wait: 0.5
$Velocity: 1000
$Lifetime: 16
+Weapon Range: 12000
# The base armor type `RTS Base Hull` scales exactly one damage type, and the
# retype list in fs2rts-capital-beams-wep.tbm only covers RETAIL weapon names
# by name. A new mod weapon is not caught by that list, so this entry has to
# carry the damage type itself or a 12,000 m beam hits command stations at full
# damage - the uncapped-beam solo-kill that file exists to prevent.
$Damage Type: RTS Capital Beam
#End
